#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553622} :activity/id #uuid "fe374825-8a1a-535d-a02b-b4ac26a4d7a8" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050770 :topic/id #uuid "6550b696-b7fd-5957-83f4-7ee02f7386ff" :topic/math-academy-id 3278} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553615 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553538 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1331e652-c61f-5c8e-a6f4-74a3f821bc65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552901} {:answer/id #uuid "1f0d9999-e6b0-5c01-ba6c-7b00ae306da2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552925} {:answer/id #uuid "3aab75be-ac8f-51df-a5c8-7c427cf91fca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552986} {:answer/id #uuid "47f5a809-544a-582b-a596-10978b78f520" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553018} {:answer/id #uuid "b897c736-6978-5c1a-82c7-2ca2fd4d1abc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553235}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186552986} :answer-field/id #uuid "3919e73a-7fa3-5959-8a80-51de4cf465ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186553398}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7a667003-8ac5-5712-9785-d67340dc0f82" :question/math-academy-id "q-96300" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Σ$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: Notice that from the matrix $Σ,$ we can deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=\\sqrt{2}$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$ without solving the characteristic equation.\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-2I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-2I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-0I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]-0[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-0I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of $A{A}^{T}$): Since the first singular value is not zero, and we know the corresponding singular right vector, we can compute the first column of $U$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, we can't use the same formula to find the second column of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find a vector\n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nsuch that \n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,‖{u}_{2}‖=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nSolving ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,$ which is equivalent to\n\n$$\n-{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=0,\n$$\n\nwe get the solution \n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3a2cb110-a121-50e5-98e3-664e4716991a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553682}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553622 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167426 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f3ba74c-8cac-500b-af49-6238e7a60068" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544156} {:answer/id #uuid "26ef721e-74d4-5a10-9cf1-42944cf88c5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544175} {:answer/id #uuid "d662914b-b98e-5bb3-8d4d-7d0ed96cb841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544546} {:answer/id #uuid "f115935a-361e-5a7a-a92c-8717bff55eaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544609} {:answer/id #uuid "f6d9ca68-4ca0-505d-ba43-841000fa1d32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544627}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544546} :answer-field/id #uuid "d614d5a4-465a-5a08-aa99-77c0edc84d79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165764}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "c5b01c9e-df01-5732-898e-b56df2318316" :question/math-academy-id "q-95921" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,Σ=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{5} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Σ$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}]}^{T}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & -10 \\\\ -10 & 10\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: Notice that from the matrix $Σ,$ we can deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=2\\sqrt{5}$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$ without solving the characteristic equation.\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=20,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-20I & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & -10 \\\\ -10 & 10\\end{aligned}]-20[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-10 & -10 \\\\ -10 & -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-20I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-0I & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & -10 \\\\ -10 & 10\\end{aligned}]-0[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10 & -10 \\\\ -10 & 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-0I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of $A{A}^{T}$): Since the first singular value is not zero, and we know the corresponding singular right vector, we can compute the first column of $U$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ -3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, we can't use the same formula to find the second column of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find a vector\n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nsuch that \n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,‖{u}_{2}‖=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nSolving ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,$ which is equivalent to\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}{x}_{1}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}{x}_{2}=0,\n$$\n\nwe get a nonzero solution $[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Normalizing this vector, we finally obtain the  second column of $U:$\n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "585b7b68-1beb-5e64-886d-4e1b2b983b3e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553623}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553623 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371346 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4abfbcd5-c08f-5808-9b5a-b3b2a3ee289c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{5} & \\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{5} & -\\frac{4}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & \\frac{3}{5}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371348} {:answer/id #uuid "358df040-d692-51f0-a906-32eab5614687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371349} {:answer/id #uuid "86b9cb74-3312-5602-ab9d-d25a940ca5f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371350} {:answer/id #uuid "618d1bdc-440a-509d-b52a-908c2a390cf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371351} {:answer/id #uuid "18851003-ddbd-550d-8a79-359f4f78f2d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$V=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371352}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371350} :answer-field/id #uuid "b963a5db-95c9-59eb-9b48-d6d0b9964aae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371347}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "55a5ae95-6d34-57f1-bd0e-b30b46e5610f" :question/math-academy-id "q-96299" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $Σ$ shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 2 \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: Notice that from the matrix $Σ,$ we can deduce that ${\\sigma }_{1}=3$ and ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$ without solving the characteristic equation.\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$):\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\sigma }_{1}^{2}=9,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-9I & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & 3\\end{bmatrix}-9\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-9I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}={\\sigma }_{2}^{2}=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A-0I & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & 3\\end{bmatrix}-0\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $({A}^{T}\\,A-0I)v=0$ gives a unit eigenvector\n\n$$\n{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of $A{A}^{T}$): Since the first singular value is not zero, and we know the corresponding singular right vector, we can compute the first column of $U$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 1 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ 3\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the second singular value is ${\\sigma }_{2}=0$, we can't use the same formula to find the second column of $U.$ But we know that $U$ must be orthogonal. Hence, we must find a vector\n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nsuch that \n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,‖{u}_{2}‖=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nSolving ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0,$ which is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}{x}_{1}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}}{x}_{2}=0,\n$$\n\nwe get a nonzero solution $\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Normalizing this vector, we finally obtain the  second column of $U:$\n\n$$\n{u}_{2}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U$ and $V:$ \n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "58dd1f4d-824a-5f34-bd20-21ac3f40bf35" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553615}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553643 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167468 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9268c777-8c11-587d-8e92-8259cc5a35a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U = \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186166017} {:answer/id #uuid "f7e15010-68b8-5d13-8a05-46a57b374da6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U = \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186166018} {:answer/id #uuid "fc2c8936-40d0-5f2e-ba43-0e536ef27d59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U = \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186166019} {:answer/id #uuid "17b99567-79ed-5509-87ab-eb0df57a874c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U = \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186166020} {:answer/id #uuid "72c5e15c-eedb-5f25-92a3-1e3649c0988a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U = \\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186166021}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e0bcae68-fbd0-5a05-8b00-13903f399796" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186166016} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bcdf095-24d5-524e-a65f-5181417d7108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371396} {:answer/id #uuid "a36e3fb8-0798-5fac-b30e-79b68bcb9da3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371397} {:answer/id #uuid "0613b5f9-b7a8-5e0a-8948-a76dbc898851" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371398} {:answer/id #uuid "23aabe88-e989-5349-bdf7-ed4b2fa1fddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371399} {:answer/id #uuid "1e38ffeb-f446-56e6-8a85-25b39aa0c303" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371400}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371396} :answer-field/id #uuid "11bf1f45-5128-5bda-8f96-b6a315da1dcd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371395}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5cc513bc-fe77-5e9e-887b-62058a8b7f56" :question/math-academy-id "q-96434" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: Notice that since ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is diagonal, the singular values of $A$ are \n\n$\\,$ ${\\sigma }_{1}={\\sigma }_{2}=1.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$): Seeking non-zero solutions of $({A}^{T}\\,A-1I)v=0,$ we obtain the unit eigenvectors \n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U,$ $Σ,$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "87a52191-3101-58ef-a6bb-fa008fb74e7a"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553682 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371388 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90fb4001-d74b-5e2d-81b4-e24b882a4776" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371390} {:answer/id #uuid "71ce610f-82ae-522c-926e-b7c2ee6f0d39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371391} {:answer/id #uuid "4b580747-f003-59f3-9a6e-264464d07479" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371392} {:answer/id #uuid "cde90a24-0864-55d6-88d1-1399a2d4ca92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371393} {:answer/id #uuid "8a2ea819-e496-5d30-a827-efe68e69aeae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$U=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{bmatrix}$ and $V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371394}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371393} :answer-field/id #uuid "db5a28ad-71bd-5130-9bc2-0a90bb411ead" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371389}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c0e502e2-3a05-5080-ba55-d3ba7ba5d628" :question/math-academy-id "q-96427" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix shown above. Given that $A=UΣ{V}^{T}$ is a singular value decomposition of $A,$ which of the following could be the matrices $U$ and $V?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the singular value decomposition of $A$ using the usual algorithm.\n\n- **Step 1.** Compute ${A}^{T}\\,A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A & ={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & \\sqrt{5} \\\\ -\\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- **Step 2.** Find the singular values: Notice that since ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is diagonal, the singular values of $A$ are \n\n$\\,$ ${\\sigma }_{1}={\\sigma }_{2}=\\sqrt{6}.$\n\n- **Step 3.** Find the right singular vectors of $A$ (i.e., the unit eigenvectors of ${A}^{T}\\,A$): Seeking non-zero solutions of $({A}^{T}\\,A-6I)v=0,$ we obtain the unit eigenvectors \n\n$\\,$ ${v}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,$ and $\\,{v}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\n- **Step 4.** Find the left singular vectors of $A$: Since we know the singular values and right singular vectors, we can compute the columns of $U$ as follows:\n\n- First, we compute ${u}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{1}}A{v}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we compute ${u}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{{\\sigma }_{2}}A{v}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -\\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we construct the matrices $U,$ $Σ,$ and $V:$\n\n$$\nU=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{6}}\\end{bmatrix},\\,Σ=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{6} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{bmatrix},\\,V=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "f52cf900-2792-505e-b166-a75202379c51" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186553643}}] :activity/title "Singular Value Decomposition of 2x2 Matrices With Zero or Repeated Eigenvalues" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186552868}]}
